# OKX v5 REST responses, written from the documented codes (read 2026-10-17).
# Not captured from a live session; numbers are made up and messages
# shortened. OKX documents the body codes, not the HTTP status: only 50011's
# 429 is stated ("HTTP 429"), and 50011 often arrives as 200 as well. The
# other statuses here are the ones these tests exercise, not a claim about
# what OKX sends. OKX sends no usage headers. Requests went out at server
# time 1700000000000 ms.
# - Rate limits: https://www.okx.com/docs-v5/en/#overview-rate-limits
# - Place order: https://www.okx.com/docs-v5/en/#order-book-trading-trade-post-place-order

### order-ok
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

{"code":"0","msg":"","data":[{"clOrdId":"b15","ordId":"312269865356374016","tag":"","ts":"1700000000000","sCode":"0","sMsg":""}],"inTime":"1700000000000000","outTime":"1700000000001000"}

### rate-limit-50011
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: application/json

{"code":"50011","msg":"Rate limit reached.","data":[]}

### sub-account-50061
HTTP/1.1 429 Too Many Requests
Content-Type: application/json

{"code":"50061","msg":"Sub-account rate limit exceeded.","data":[]}

### timestamp-50102
HTTP/1.1 401 Unauthorized
Content-Type: application/json

{"code":"50102","msg":"Timestamp request expired.","data":[]}

### timeout-50004
HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
Content-Type: application/json

{"code":"50004","msg":"API endpoint request timeout (does not mean that the request was successful or failed, please check the request result).","data":[]}

### order-failed-1
HTTP/1.1 200 OK
Content-Type: application/json

{"code":"1","msg":"All operations failed","data":[{"clOrdId":"b15","ordId":"","tag":"","ts":"1700000000000","sCode":"51008","sMsg":"Order failed. Insufficient balance."}],"inTime":"1700000000000000","outTime":"1700000000001000"}

### unavailable-503
